', '', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'spiritual ethos the discourse to kumayl', 'the discourse to kumayl on a night outside kufa ali ibn abi talib peace be upon him led one disciple by the hand to a graveyard drew a deep breath and confided a counsel that later generations treated as one of the most esoteric in the whole tradition this episode recites that discourse to kumayl whole the three types of people knowledge weighed above wealth the abundant knowledge in his own breast and the rare guardians of the proof through whom knowledge penetrates the reality of insight and then follows the commentary into what it teaches knowledge it argues must storm past the surface of words into the heart past the zahir into the batin the warlike verb hajama makes the passage vivid that penetration cannot happen unless the whole soul is won for the intellect which is the greatest struggle the battle for the nafs against hawa and the subtle idolatry of the ego its aim is integration tawhid and its ground is ikhlas sincerity made purely for god sustained by worship closing on the command to worship until certainty comes', '');
